>3) Some corpses are tainted and will kill.  How do I avoid this?

Corpses tend to rot if you let them sit too long.  If you have any
plans to eat a corpse, your best bet is to eat it right after slaying
the monster, lest it start to decay.  Note that corpses left by
zombies, mummies, &c. are already old, though not immediately
inedible.  If you do get sickened by a rotten corpse, you might either
#pray or apply a unicorn horn.  Using a unicorn horn is much more
reliable, but you can't always find one when you need it.

>4) What does the message "You have a strange feeling for a moment.  Then it
>passes." mean?  I get this from scrolls and potions.

It means the scroll or potion did something not immediately obvious.
The most common occurrences are when you read a scroll of {food,gold}
detection and the only food or gold on the level is that which you're
carrying.  Note this is to be distinguished from the message "You have
a _p_e_c_u_l_i_a_r feeling for a moment, then it passes." which only appears
when you quaff a potion of invisibility and you already have intrinsic
see invisible.

>5) Other than pets, is there any other way to tell if an item is cursed?

Well, you could always play a priest.  Priests automatically know the
blessed/cursed status of every item they see.  For those non-priests
out there, the best way by far is to drop the item in question on an
altar.  The blessed/cursed status of the item will be instantly made
known to the character, provided he or she is not blind when the item
lands.  Note that potions of water will be changed to reflect the
alignment of the altar.  (Dropping a potion of unholy water on a
lawful altar will make it holy water, and vice versa.)

